    "source": "// The checkout from \"Automatic Concurrency Without async/await\".\n// Each item costs 300 ms to price, 200 ms to check and 100 ms to record, so\n// four items one call after another would take 2400 ms. The last line shows\n// how long the checkout took here. Try other carts: \"gone\" is sold out, \"zz\"\n// is discontinued, and \"slow\" takes 1000 ms to price.\n\nOutOfTime! { Decimal recorded }\n\n@Pricing {}\n@Pricing.quote(String sku) -> Decimal | Discontinued! {\n    if sku == \"slow\" { r::Clock.sleep(1000ms) } else { r::Clock.sleep(300ms) }\n    if sku == \"zz\" { return Discontinued! }\n    return 1.00\n}\n\n@Inventory {}\n@Inventory.check(String sku) -> Int | Discontinued! {\n    r::Clock.sleep(200ms)\n    if sku == \"zz\" { return Discontinued! }\n    if sku == \"gone\" { return 0 }\n    return 5\n}\n\n@Ledger {}\n@Ledger.record(String sku, Decimal price) {\n    r::Clock.sleep(100ms)\n}\n\nDiscontinued!\n\nlistPrice(String sku) -> Decimal { return 1.00 }\n\ncheckout(String[] skus) -> String {\n    Decimal total = 0.00\n    Int skipped, reconcile = 0, 0\n    for sku in skus {\n        Decimal price = @Pricing.quote(sku) handle Unavailable! => listPrice(sku)\n        Int stock = @Inventory.check(sku)\n        if stock == 0 { skipped += 1; continue }\n        @Ledger.record(sku, price)\n        total += price\n    } handle {\n        Discontinued! => { skipped += 1; continue }\n        Unverified! => { reconcile += 1; continue }\n        Cancelled! => return OutOfTime! { recorded: total }\n    }\n    return f\"total ${total}, skipped {skipped}, reconcile {reconcile}\"\n}\n\nmain() {\n    DateTime start = r::Clock.time()\n    print(checkout([\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\"]))\n    Duration elapsed = r::Clock.time() - start\n    print(f\"took {Int.fromFloat(elapsed / 1ms)} ms\")\n}\n"
